            <ArticleTitle>[Valdoxan in the treatment of depression in neurological practice: results of the Russian multicenter naturalistic study &quot;Resonance&quot;].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Efficacy and tolerability of valdoxan (agomelatin) in the treatment of mild and moderate depression caused by neurologic diseases (cerebrovascular disorders, neurocirculatory dystonia, chronic pain syndrome) were studied in a sample of 277 patients aged from 18 to 70 years (mean age 46.0±11.3 years), including 21.66% men and 76.53% women. Patients received valdoxan during 6 weeks. Symptoms of depression were arrested in 81.20% of patients. There was the decrease in signs of fatigability and the improvement of work effectiveness assessed by specific tests. Coefficient of mental stability reached normal values.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
